{"base_rate":0.4242837653478854,"brier":0.1617244201909959,"bss":0.3379196293869341,"bss_hi":0.4300581860136761,"bss_lo":0.2351113199187391,"chart":{"base":[612.2,58.7],"fp":[241.0,270.1],"lead":"62,262.8 272,239.5 482,205.2 692,156.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.34 — higher than 63% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +23pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 68% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 7%; promised 100% → rained 80%"},"rel":"80.3,435 444,306.2 689.4,119.2"},"country":"NO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1416371077762619,"ess":358.73688966876114,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Kristiansand</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Kristiansand rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 733 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nKRISTIANSAND - SOMSKLEIVA, 3.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.34, ranked 78 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(45&ndash;133) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>219</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>294</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Kristiansand</b> <span class=\"muted\">Norway</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.34</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>45&ndash;133\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>733 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Kristiansand &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Kristiansand\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.87287671232877,378.675799086758 96.03108108108108,313.1351351351351 198.77913043478256,197.3623188405797 338.8553246753247,60.54545454545456 410.5310204081632,18.0 410.5310204081632,22.952380952380963 338.8553246753247,122.0 198.77913043478256,276.4927536231884 96.03108108108108,367.2432432432432 58.87287671232877,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"227.5607094133697\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"227.5607094133697\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.87287671232877,367.041095890411 96.03108108108108,322.97297297297297 198.77913043478256,276.4927536231884 338.8553246753247,221.27272727272728 410.5310204081632,89.8095238095238\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 219 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.87287671232877\" cy=\"367.041095890411\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"96.03108108108108\" cy=\"322.97297297297297\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 40%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"198.77913043478256\" cy=\"276.4927536231884\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 79%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"338.8553246753247\" cy=\"221.27272727272728\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 294 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.5310204081632\" cy=\"89.8095238095238\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Kristiansand the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.21).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>151</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.208</td><td class='num'>15.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.344</td><td class='num'>14.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'>0.369</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.377</td><td class='num'>13.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":58.14671,"lon":7.9956,"n":733,"n_cities":213,"name":"Kristiansand","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0024657534246575346,"n":219,"obs":0.0410958904109589,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2360000000000002,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.10743243243243242,"n":74,"obs":0.16216216216216217,"sig":false},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.2360000000000002,"mean":0.39768115942028975,"n":69,"obs":0.2898550724637681,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.7933766233766234,"n":77,"obs":0.44155844155844154,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9958503401360543,"n":294,"obs":0.8027210884353742,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.4,"provisional":false,"rank":78,"rank_hi":133.0,"rank_lo":44.975,"reliability":0.029805355945818828,"resolution":0.10998065930349643,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"kristiansand","station":"KRIST